.TH VTIUM\-GALLERY 1 2026-11-17 "vtium 0.1.0-alpha.9" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vtium-gallery \- show PNG pictures as thumbnails in a terminal that supports kitty graphics
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBvtium\-gallery\fR [\fB\-s\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-n\fR \fIN\fR] [\fI\-L\fR] [\fB\-w\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-probe\fR] [\fIFILE\fR|\fIDIR\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows PNG pictures as a grid of thumbnails, each with its file name under it, in a terminal that draws kitty graphics: kitty, WezTerm, Ghostty or vtium. A directory stands for the files in it, in name order, and no arguments means the current directory. The terminal scales each picture, so the tool sends PNG files as they are and skips any other file with a note.
.PP
A build of vtium with image support installs the program as \fBvtium\-gallery\fR. The program is a bash script, and needs only bash and the usual base tools.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-size\fR \fIN\fR
thumbnail height in rows (default 8); a square picture is about 2N columns wide
.TP
\fB\-n\fR \fIN\fR
show the first N pictures, and say how many more there are
.TP
\fI\-L\fR, \fB\-\-no\-labels\fR
leave out the file names
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-wait\fR \fIN\fR
wait up to N seconds for the terminal to answer the question (default 1); a terminal at the far end of a slow link can need longer
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-probe\fR
draw without first asking the terminal whether it draws kitty graphics, and take its cells to be twice as tall as they are wide
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
print the usage and exit
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
vtium-gallery showed the pictures, or printed its usage.
.TP
1
vtium-gallery found no PNG picture, or the terminal did not answer that it supports kitty graphics.
.TP
2
The command line is wrong, or a file or directory it names does not exist.
.SH SEE ALSO
vtium(8)
